    "summary": "Root cause: the accepted decision structure.system was \"simply_supported\", but the bridge is a single continuous unit of three spans (20+25+20 m) built as precast girders made continuous. Per MR-05, with three spans and no pier-column geometry given (support 1 is merely named \"Pier\", pier instance is null), the system must be \"continuous\". The wrong system produced a spurious check failure.\n\nRepair: re-proposed structure.system = \"continuous\" (evidence MR-05) and re-ran the modal analysis. f1 = 5.573 Hz, unchanged, so lane.mu = 0.1767·ln(f1) − 0.0157 = 0.2879 (JTGD60-4.3.2) remained valid; girder.w and girder.m are system-independent (MR-07) and unchanged.\n\nResult: generate_model now passes its L1/L2/L3 checks. Model: 2D spine-beam, 3-span continuous (20/25/20 m), 4 precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C50, A=4.242 m², I=1.007 m⁴ per section, self-weight only). Bearings: PTFE sliding laminated elastomeric (8 per line) at abutments 0 and 3 and pier 2, plain laminated elastomeric fixed (8 per line) at pier 1. Key results: self-weight reactions 820/2764/2764/820 kN; self-weight midspan moments ≈2690/2968/2690 kN·m with support moments ≈ −5649 kN·m; governing lane (Class I) max positive moment 5341 kN·m and max negative moment −3864 kN·m; fundamental vertical frequency 5.573 Hz, impact factor μ = 0.288."
